{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"81c950c6-3008-402e-8816-56424b15c67d","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Similar triangles have equal corresponding angles. Here, the smaller right triangle has side lengths three, four, and five.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"Similar triangles"},{"op":"diagram","id":"triangles","region":"left","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.12,0.07],[0.12,0.29]],"stroke":"solid","label":"3"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.12,0.29],[0.44,0.29]],"stroke":"solid","label":"4"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.44,0.29],[0.12,0.07]],"stroke":"solid","label":"5"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.12,0.265],[0.147,0.265],[0.147,0.29]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"right angle in the smaller triangle"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"81c950c6-3008-402e-8816-56424b15c67d","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Enlarge every side by two. The new triangle has the same shape, with corresponding sides six, eight, and ten.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"large_vertical","canvas_id":"triangles","from":[0.12,0.44],"to":[0.12,0.88],"stroke":"solid","label":"6"},{"op":"line","id":"large_base","canvas_id":"triangles","from":[0.12,0.88],"to":[0.76,0.88],"stroke":"solid","label":"8"},{"op":"line","id":"large_hyp","canvas_id":"triangles","from":[0.76,0.88],"to":[0.12,0.44],"stroke":"solid","label":"10"},{"op":"arrow","id":"scale","canvas_id":"triangles","from":[0.82,0.2],"to":[0.82,0.65],"stroke":"solid","label":"×2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"81c950c6-3008-402e-8816-56424b15c67d","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Compare matching sides in the same order. Every larger-to-smaller ratio equals two: that common ratio is the scale factor.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"ratios","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\frac{6}{3}=\\frac{8}{4}=\\frac{10}{5}=2"},{"op":"text","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"ratios","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Matching sides share one scale factor."},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"large_right","canvas_id":"triangles","center":[0.12,0.88],"radius":0.045,"start_deg":-90,"end_deg":0,"stroke":"solid","label":"90°"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the side corresponding to 4 becomes 12, what does the side corresponding to 5 become?","expected_gist":"The scale factor is 3, so the corresponding side becomes 15."}}}
